# No unrequested commits (Cursor agents)

This rule applies to **Cursor** agents in this workspace (`.cursor/rules/`). It is not a repo-wide contributor policy for other tools or humans.

Leave all work in the local working tree for human review unless the user **explicitly** asks to commit and/or push.

## Never treat these as commit permission

- Executing or “building” a plan (Plan → Build, “implement the plan”, “execute the plan”, “do the todos”)
- Finishing implementation, tests passing, or “land this on main” phrased as an outcome in a plan
- Opening or updating a PR description without an explicit commit/push request
- Phrases like “done”, “ship it” about **code completeness** without the words commit / push / PR create

## Required before any git commit

The user must clearly ask to commit (e.g. “commit this”, “create a commit”, “commit and push”). Same for push and for creating a PR that needs a push.

## After plan execution

Stop with a short summary of what changed and which files to review. Do **not** `git add`, `git commit`, or `git push` as part of wrapping up.

## Related

Do not remove or narrow this rule unless the user asked to delete or replace it (see `no-unrequested-deletions`).
